ns ARE Silver Ladder in the picture. Believing in greater power, empowering kids, working with dedication on unification of society at their moral guidance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:38:35-07:00","id":974515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974496#post974496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? the ones i hung around with were super sweet to me :&gt;,maybe it's american nuns thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know. I haven't actually been around very many nuns, my experience is all second hand from my parents who were raised Catholic and had some pretty bad experiences in Catholic school. In hindsight that was maybe not the most tasteful joke, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:39:09-07:00","id":974516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974515#post974515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I don't know. I haven't actually been around very many nuns; my experience is all second hand. In hindsight that was maybe not the most tasteful joke, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>ah its okay :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:41:26-07:00","id":974517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974461#post974461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover of the Silver Ladder book. Was always one of the more bizarre Mage covers to me in Awakening 1E.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn1.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQ8YDa5NmVbI10SO2cCgFNejXc2HwhOIUnzYyLDQIPq-Mo-IrPvHfkQUfZV\" target=\"_blank\">https://encrypted-tbn1.gstatic.com/i...o-IrPvHfkQUfZV</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I love that picture so much. I'm also a big fan of the Transhuman Engineers illustration featuring a white Geek Squad employee from the Free Council, pointing earnestly at a pile of random computer parts on the ground in a generic indigenous village while the locals stare in confusion. And while we're on the topic, can we talk about the 2E Adamantine Arrow art of Baron Mordo and Skeletor plotting how to destroy He-Man once and for all? I'm just really into art that depicts CofD protagonists as ridiculous/laughable/absurd, and all of the 2E Order art pretty much hits it out of the park there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:48:49-07:00","id":974525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974517#post974517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. And while we're on the topic, can we talk about the 2E Adamantine Arrow art of Baron Mordo and Skeletor plotting how to destroy He-Man once and for all?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the naked beefcake jawa art! I love that piece, but it really looks like something out of a completely different game. Maybe the artist thought they were doing something for Asenscion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:59:20-07:00","id":974537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974525#post974525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the naked beefcake jawa art! I love that piece, but it really looks like something out of a completely different game. Maybe the artist thought they were doing something for Asenscion.</div> </div> </div> </div>its just such a weak point for this book,its hard to see the orders as this an cient traditions who held amazing knowledge and power when they are represented by those guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:20:44-07:00","id":974551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974537#post974537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its just such a weak point for this book,its hard to see the orders as this an cient traditions who held amazing knowledge and power when they are represented by those guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm not sure what's going on in most of them. The two that really succeed for me are the Mysterium Art and the Seers of the Throne art. Both get the feel of their respective Orders across to me very effectively. The Free Council art I have mixed feelings about, it could be better, but I get what it was going for and I'm cool with it. The Guardians of the Veil art is uninspiring to me, but doesn't particularly bother me. Again, it could be better but it could also be worse. The Silver Ladder art I'm with you on, I have no idea what is happening there or what it has to do with the Order in question. I absolutely love the Adamantine Arrow art, for completely the wrong reasons. It makes me laugh, which is the surest way to earn my approval, but it doesn't do anything to communicate to me what the Arrow is about, and if anything, leaves me with the impression that the Arrow are a bunch of silver age comic book supervillains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:05:01-07:00","id":974573,"title":"","content":"My first thought on seeing the Silver Ladder piece is that all 3 of the women are with the Ladder. They represent two different aspects of the Order, the Nuns are the shepherds guiding their charges towards enlightenment, the Suit with a check is the politicking Powerbroker who gets what she wants. I like the stuff for the Paths much more but just really wish we had more art overall , .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:08:30-07:00","id":974577,"title":"","content":"I think the average level of the interior art in the 2E core is on balance higher than that of the 1E core but there are some serious rough patches and it is a real shame that the Order pieces are among them. I mean, they're not on the level of Silver Ladder iPod guy with rickets, but while they're mostly fine pieces on their own merits, I don't think many convey the vibe of their respective Orders very well at all. The Path art is by contrast much better communicated even if a couple of the illustrations are a bit rubbery in that Photoshoppy digital media way - the figures are clear and communicate something.<br /> <br /> There are random bits of interior art throughout the book where I'm just like lol, like the guy who is SUPER STOKED to be talking to a rat, but some of it's fantastic and the chapter opening pieces are uniformly gorgeous. They communicate the vibe of the game perfectly, with flat planes of color broken up by formal, geometric compositions that call to mind hieroglyphs and stained glass and architectural drawings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:38:03-07:00","id":974670,"title":"","content":"To be fair to the SL frog-man, he was the first person I ever saw wearing their i-pod in their breast pocket. For that service I thank him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:48:38-07:00","id":974678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974551#post974551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I'm not sure what's going on in most of them. The two that really succeed for me are the Mysterium Art and the Seers of the Throne art. Both get the feel of their respective Orders across to me very effectively. The Free Council art I have mixed feelings about, it could be better, but I get what it was going for and I'm cool with it. The Guardians of the Veil art is uninspiring to me, but doesn't particularly bother me. Again, it could be better but it could also be worse. The Silver Ladder art I'm with you on, I have no idea what is happening there or what it has to do with the Order in question. I absolutely love the Adamantine Arrow art, for completely the wrong reasons. It makes me laugh, which is the surest way to earn my approval, but it doesn't do anything to communicate to me what the Arrow is about, and if anything, leaves me with the impression that the Arrow are a bunch of silver age comic book supervillains.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm surprised that there's not more discussion about the Seer or Free Council art. When the Mage PDF was first released, those two pieces generated considerable debate. I recall that the Seer art seemed like a homage to Eyes Wide shut, and was very evocative and totally appropriate for the Order. I wasn't too impressed by the Seer &quot;San Francisco pride parade&quot; art. I understood the intention, but it seemed to really miss an opportunity to portray the ancient and modern mix and diversity in the order, and seemed more like a gratuitous political statement that the Order was liberal, rather than their belief in democracy and the magic of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:05:55-07:00","id":974688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974678#post974678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that there's not more discussion about the Seer or Free Council art. When the Mage PDF was first released, those two pieces generated considerable debate. I recall that the Seer art seemed like a homage to Eyes Wide shut, and was very evocative and totally appropriate for the Order. I wasn't too impressed by the Seer &amp;quot;San Francisco pride parade&amp;quot; art. I understood the intention, but it seemed to really miss an opportunity to portray the ancient and modern mix and diversity in the order, and seemed more like a gratuitous political statement that the Order was liberal, rather than their belief in democracy and the magic of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seer one seems pretty polarizing. People either love it or hate it, and they seem to fall along similar lines to the &quot;Are the Seers complex antagonists?&quot; debate. The arguments about the Free Council art I always felt were kind of overblown. It's not as perfect a thumbnail of the Order it stands for as the Seer art is, but it's not a bad representation. It's a clear case of &quot;could have been better, could have been worse&quot;, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:55:09-07:00","id":974711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974678#post974678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that there's not more discussion about the Seer or Free Council art. When the Mage PDF was first released, those two pieces generated considerable debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Said 'considerable debate' encompassed the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974537#post974537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its just such a weak point for this book,its hard to see the orders as this an cient traditions who held amazing knowledge and power when they are represented by those guys</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's not that many kinds of people who would wear such things, and while one of those kinds of people are cosplayers, another are people so powerful it doesn't matter what they wear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:40:11-07:00","id":974777,"title":"","content":"The Seer one is homage to The Invisibles, where the Outer Church (who the Seers are largely based on) host a soiree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:53:14-07:00","id":974786,"title":"","content":"If I was going to do a picture for the Silver Ladder, I'd probably go for something a bit more simple, but hopefully evocative. Something like, a man covered in Abyssal scars and tattoos, in shackles, stands in front of a group of wizards while a man in rather average business attire obviously defends him. Basically trying to show that the Ladder places the Lex Magica and their Traditions above their own feelings. Another obvious one would be a Silver Ladder mentoring a Sleeper as they read a Grimoire or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:17:14-07:00","id":974868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974777#post974777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seer one is homage to The Invisibles, <b>where the Outer Church (who the Seers are largely based on)</b> host a soiree.</div> </div> </div> </div>SWEET VINDICATION","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:22:43-07:00","id":975229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974517#post974517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And while we're on the topic, can we talk about the 2E Adamantine Arrow art of Baron Mordo and Skeletor plotting how to destroy He-Man once and for all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god you owe me a new keyboard...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:13:08-07:00","id":976040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=974777#post974777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seer one is homage to The Invisibles, where the Outer Church (who the Seers are largely based on) host a soiree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. And here was me thinking it was a nod to Eyes Wide Shut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:46:33-07:00","id":976165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=976040#post976040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. And here was me thinking it was a nod to Eyes Wide Shut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secret, quasi-religious societies of phenomenally wealthy people engaging in clandestine debauched and highly depraved parties (particularly where a servant unexpectedly dies) is a trope that existed well before The Invisibles or Eyes Wide Shut. However, as a matter of popular culture, far more people would recognize and associate a major Tom Cruise movie like EWS than a comic such as The Invisibles.<br /> <br /> However, in the CofD, was Stanley Kubrick a Seer, and did he really die after EWS or just ascend to join his Exarch masters? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:11:05-07:00","id":976177,"title":"","content":"Wasn't so much that, but their manner of dress and masks, but point taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:47:53-07:00","id":976192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=976177#post976177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't so much that, but their manner of dress and masks, but point taken.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The manner of dress and masks really wasn't that original or remarkable. They were typical of those type of &quot;secret society of rich people parties&quot; in media and literature.<br /> <br /> I, too, associated the Seer art with Eyes Wide Shut. Regardless, of whether the actual homage was EWS or the Invisibles, they both convey the same tenor and themes, and thus the Seer art was no doubt an excellent choice for the book (and far better and more evocative than the jawas and gay pride parade).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T18:45:25-07:00","id":976232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974430-the-silver-ladder-picture?p=976192#post976192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The manner of dress and masks really wasn't that original or remarkable. They were typical of those type of &quot;secret society of rich people parties&quot; in media and literature<br /> <br /> I, too, associated the Seer art with Eyes Wide Shut. Regardless, of whether the actual homage was EWS or the Invisibles, they both convey the same tenor and themes, and thus the Seer art was no doubt an excellent choice for the book (and far better and more evocative than the jawas and gay pride parade).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've he got a big problem with the seer picture too actually. It isn't Threatening at all. This pic shows them partying it shows the reward they had for their service to the Exarchs,but we never see what they did to earn all those earthly pleasures. The Seers are supposed to be a threat,to be somethings mages are wary of,or even downright terrified enoughl When I look at the seer image I just see people having a party,not dping anything important or significant. why the hell would any pentacle mage feel even a little bit afraid of the people on the seer drawing? How are they even a little bit threatening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:52:37-07:00","id":976349,"title":"","content":"Crucifying a guy isn't threatening? The part that should be threatening to a Pentacle Mage is the blatant display of wealth, anyone who can throw six figures away on a 'gesture' is someone to be taken serious.<br /> \u200bPersonally I would have opted for panels of two or three pictures to represent each order. For the Silver Ladder I would have done a panel with a charismatic man in an expensive suit breaking ground on a community college or rehab center, something that will help uplift Sleepers, then I would have had a scene were Mage lawyers were debating law, followed by twenty somethings engaged in community activism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:53:49-07:00","id":976350,"title":"","content":"They have an actual crucified dude as decoration...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:19:29-07:00","id":976384,"title":"","content":"They quite clearly have more power than they know what to do with and no empathy for other human beings. That should be plenty of reason to be afraid of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:15:10-07:00","id":976814,"title":"","content":"To me, the Seer picture says that they only authority that can bring you to heel is the Exarchs. And the list of things they don't give a shit about is long and dark, so long as you are loyal to their commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidyga